## Liquibase verifys connection
liquibase status

## Liquibase validates changelog and environment
liquibase validate

## Liquibase creates a snapshot of the current database
liquibase --output-file=schema-snap.json snapshot --snapshot-format=json

## Liquibase diffs environments with objects specified 
liquibase diff --diff-types=tables,indexes,views

## Liquibase generate change from difference
liquibase diff-changelog --changelog-file=example-changelog2.xml

## Liquibase shows the SQL that would apply the generated changelog
liquibase update-sql --changelog-file=example-changelog2.xml  --output-file=example-changelog2.sql

## Liquibase applies the changes from the changelog to the database
liquibase update --changelog-file=example-changelog2.xml

## Liquibase tags the current state for future rollback
liquibase tag v1.0-after-update

## Liquibase rolls back the most recent changeSet
liquibase rollbackCount 1 --changelog-file=example-changelog.sql

## Liquibase rolls back to a specific tag (must have been tagged earlier)
liquibase rollback v1.0-after-update --changelog-file=example-changelog1.xml

## Rollback to a previously tagged state
liquibase rollback v1.0-after-update --changelog-file=example-changelog.xml

## Liquibase shows SQL to roll back a specific changeset (must include <rollback>)
liquibase rollback-one-changeset-sql \
  --changeSetId=NameHerE \
  --changeSetAuthor=benriley \
  --changeSetPath=example-changelog.sql


## Roll back a specific changeset by ID and author
liquibase rollbackOneChangeSet \
  --changeSetId=12345 \
  --changeSetAuthor=benriley \
  --changeSetPath=example-changelog1.xml

## liquibase xml labels and context
labels: descriptive tags (e.g. release, dev-only)
context: environment-specific control (e.g. prod, dev)

<changeSet id="001" author="benriley" labels="dev,test" context="dev">
    <addColumn tableName="user">
        <column name="debug_mode" type="BOOLEAN" defaultValueBoolean="false"/>
    </addColumn>
</changeSet>

liquibase update --label-filter=dev
liquibase update --contexts=dev

## Liquibase Use runAlways and runOnChange wisely
<changeSet id="002" author="benriley" runAlways="true">
    <update tableName="config">
        <column name="last_modified" valueDate="NOW()"/>
        <where>id=1</where>
    </update>
</changeSet>

runAlways="true": runs every time Liquibase executes (good for reference data).
runOnChange="true": runs again only if the content of the changeset changes.

## Liquibase Pre-conditions
Use preConditions to protect environments

<changeSet id="003" author="benriley">
    <preConditions onFail="HALT">
        <not>
            <columnExists tableName="customer" columnName="email"/>
        </not>
    </preConditions>

    <addColumn tableName="customer">
        <column name="email" type="VARCHAR(255)"/>
    </addColumn>
</changeSet>

🧠 Why:
Prevents double-adding columns or applying changes in the wrong context.

